<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="058" project="spaarkeai-compose-r8">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-A10 residual - carry NESTED / conditional fields, the shape real templates use; retire the nested/unterminated row</title>
    <phase>4 Track A - Fidelity</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes the projection's field scanner - the component that decides what a field IS. Mis-reconstructing a nested instruction authors a DIFFERENT field: a document-correctness defect, not a cosmetic one.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Capability-matched: task 049 flattened nested fields for a STRUCTURAL reason, not laziness. `FieldScanState` folds an inner field into the outer span, so the only recoverable instruction is a CONCATENATION of outer and inner instruction text; re-emitting it authors a different field. The work is deciding whether the scanner can preserve the field TREE without destabilising the flat scan every other carried class depends on - and, if it cannot, saying so honestly instead of shipping a plausible reconstruction.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Same save spine as 049/056/070-073.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>049, 057</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, compose, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Owner decision 2026-08-25, answering "we will be introducing templates and field-merge-codes, will these
    be supported?" - simple merge codes already are; conditional ones are not, and that gap must close.

    Task 049's gate is structural, so MERGEFIELD is carried VERBATIM today under "unknown / vendor
    instruction: carry, never interpret". That half works.

    What does NOT work is the shape real templates actually use - a conditional merge block, an IF field
    whose condition and result both contain MERGEFIELDs. Task 049 flattens it, by design and for a real
    reason recorded in notes/049-field-carry-decisions.md section 2: FieldScanState folds the inner field
    into the outer span (MaxDepth greater than 1), so the only instruction it can recover is a CONCATENATION
    of the outer and inner instruction text. Re-emitting that authors a DIFFERENT field - worse than
    flattening, because it looks like it worked.

    So this is not "remove a guard". The scanner has to preserve the field TREE - outer instruction, inner
    fields, and the result span - without destabilising the flat scan every other carried class depends on
    (REF, PAGEREF, PAGE, SEQ, STYLEREF, HYPERLINK, vendor). TOC and INDEX stay OUT of scope: they span
    paragraph marks, so begin and end sit in different containers and there is no complete field to carry.

    The honest outcome if the tree cannot be preserved safely is to keep flattening and say so on the
    published list, with the template implication stated plainly - the owner needs to know before authoring
    templates, not after. Do not ship a reconstruction you cannot prove round-trips.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE backend developer. Expert in ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder's field scanner, ComposeField, and ComposeDocumentRenderer.AppendField.</role>

  <goal>
    A conditional merge field in a paragraph the user edits round-trips as the SAME field - outer
    instruction, nested inner fields and lock/dirty flags intact - or the published list states honestly
    that it does not, with the consequence for template authoring named.
  </goal>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="task 049">A carried instruction MUST reproduce the SAME field. A concatenated instruction is not a carry, it is a silent substitution.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 049">MUST NOT destabilise the flat scan the already-carried classes depend on. Those are shipped and covered by ComposeFieldCarrySeamTests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-049 I-5">One body author. Re-emit inside ComposeDocumentRenderer.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project invariant 1">An unreconstructable field degrades to today's flatten plus named warning - never a refusal.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-A10">Move the row only when the parity test proves it, in BOTH directions.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md section 10">Publish size vs the 43.74 MB current / 60 MB ceiling; no new NuGet; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Seam test over a REAL corpus document containing a nested merge field. The corpus has none - add one; task 056 added inline-image.docx the same way via tests/fixtures/compose-corpus/generators/.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare FULL. Read notes/049-field-carry-decisions.md section 2 FIRST - it explains why this was flattened, and that reasoning is the thing to defeat or confirm.</step>
    <step order="1">Add a nested-merge-field corpus fixture plus generator.</step>
    <step order="2">Decide whether FieldScanState can preserve the tree. If not, STOP and report - that is a legitimate outcome.</step>
    <step order="3">Failing seam test FIRST, observed to fail, then implement.</step>
    <step order="4">Prove the already-carried classes are unaffected - the flat-scan non-regression.</step>
    <step order="5">Update the residual list plus parity family; publish-size and CVE report.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If preserving the field tree destabilises the flat scan for the shipped classes, STOP. Those carries are live and proven; trading them for nested support is a net loss.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a nested field can only be carried by reconstructing an instruction that is not byte-identical to the source, STOP and keep flattening. A field that looks carried but behaves differently is the worst outcome available.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDocxProjectionBuilder.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeContentModel.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeDocumentRenderer.cs</output>
    <output type="doc">docs/architecture/COMPOSE-WRITE-RESIDUAL-LOSS.md</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/Compose/</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>A conditional merge field in an EDITED paragraph round-trips as the same field, asserted through the real renderer over a real fixture - OR the flatten is retained and the list says so with the template consequence named.</criterion>
    <criterion>Every already-carried field class still round-trips (flat-scan non-regression).</criterion>
    <criterion>Every test observed to FAIL before its fix.</criterion>
    <criterion>Residual list and parity agree in both directions.</criterion>
    <criterion>NEGATIVE: no reconstructed instruction that differs from the source.</criterion>
    <criterion>Publish size reported; no new NuGet; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
